      "content": [
        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "**Yes. One cost event for manufacturing order MO-25-09-1070 was created 75 minutes after the September cost period entered Pending Close. Its recorded `POSTED` status is inconsistent with Oracle’s documented treatment for this transaction type.**\n\n### Event identified\n\n| Item | Finding |\n|---|---|\n| Operation | Modine Racine — Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Source transaction | **TXN-ISSUE-250930-1070** |\n| Cost event | `CE-250904-0004` — `INPUT` / component issue |\n| Amount | **US$284,763.42** — 28,476,342 cents |\n| Cost period | `Sep-25` / `PER-COST-2025-09` |\n| Exact event-created time | **2025-09-30T19:15:00** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Time after Pending Close | **75 minutes — 1 hour 15 minutes** |\n| Recorded accounting status | **POSTED** |\n\nCalculation: `19:15:00 − 18:00:00 = 4,500 seconds ÷ 60 = 75 minutes`.\n\n*The timestamps are reproduced exactly as stored; the source records do not specify a time zone.*\n\n### Policy assessment\n\nOracle’s **“Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting”** section states that new transactions created after a period enters Pending Close, relating to that period or an earlier period, **will not be staged or processed until the period is closed or reopened**. The documented exceptions are revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments.\n\nThis event is a **new component issue dated September 30**, not one of those exceptions. Therefore, its **`POSTED` status is not consistent** with the documented Pending Close treatment in the supplied records.\n\n**Sources:** `work_orders`, `cost_periods`, and `work_order_cost_events` in `system/oracle_scm_cost_management/state.db`; Oracle Cost Management 26B documentation, printed page **225** / PDF page **233**.\n\nThe review was read-only; **no database records were changed**. The audit result and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_85c0bb4450b2/audit-report.json`.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
